{
  "_comment": "Target-company registry for ats-watch. Each entry: {ats, slug, name, tags}. Add companies freely — the CLI polls whatever is listed here. To find a company's ATS, try its careers page URL: jobs.ashbyhq.com/<slug>, boards.greenhouse.io/<slug>, jobs.lever.co/<slug>, apply.workable.com/api/v1/widget/accounts/<slug> (no description field — a Workable job's description will always come back null, that's the API's limit, not a bug), api.smartrecruiters.com/v1/companies/<slug>/postings, <slug>.recruitee.com/api/offers/. Large remote-jobs marketplace boards (intermediaries that list on behalf of other employers) are deliberately not registered: they tend to time out and they hide the real hiring company, which makes the Sector Gate unverifiable. Bulk growth via probe_slugs.py, which verifies each slug against every supported vendor with a live request; see that script's docstring for per-vendor probe reliability. Recruitee was added as the 6th ATS type after a strong-fit role on a vanity careers domain (jobs.<company>.com over Recruitee) was missed entirely. Recruitee 404s properly on unknown slugs, so it is a reliable probe. NOTE for Recruitee entries: the top-level `location` is a display string (\"Remote job\"); real geography lives in `locations[]`, which the CLI joins. Tags are free-form hints for humans (sector, region, how the entry was discovered); the CLI does not filter on them.",
